---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="News & Events">
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>News & Events</h1>
      <p class="breadcrumb"><a href={base}>Home</a> / News & Events</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="content">
    <div class="container">
      <p>
        Stay updated with the latest news, events, and developments from the DEUCE project.
      </p>

      <div class="news-item">
        <h2>Project Launch</h2>
        <p class="event-date">2024</p>

        <p>
          The DEUCE Project has officially launched, bringing together a consortium of ten partners
          from across Europe to improve the enforcement of judicial decisions in cross-border pecuniary
          claims under the European Enforcement Order (EEO) and European Order for Payment (EOP) regulations.
        </p>

        <p>
          Coordinated by the University of Naples Federico II, the project aims to address the significant
          challenges that currently hinder the effective enforcement of these EU instruments, making
          cross-border debt recovery more accessible and efficient for creditors across the European Union.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="news-item">
        <h2>DEUCE Platform Development</h2>
        <p>
          The DEUCE e-platform is being developed to provide comprehensive information on EEO and EOP
          enforcement procedures across 26 EU Member States. The platform will offer detailed roadmaps,
          interactive guides, and practical tools for legal practitioners and creditors.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://deuce.scan2project.org/home" class="btn btn-accent" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Access DEUCE Platform</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="news-item">
        <h2>Upcoming Events</h2>
        <p>
          The DEUCE consortium will be organizing stakeholder meetings, workshops, and dissemination events
          throughout the project duration. These events aim to engage with national enforcement authorities,
          legal practitioners, and other key stakeholders to validate research findings and promote the
          project's tools and outputs.
        </p>
        <p class="coming-soon">Event details coming soon</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .news-item {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .news-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .news-item h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .event-date {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .event-details {
    background: var(--color-background-alt);
    padding: 1rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }

  .event-details p {
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
  }

  .event-details p:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .event-details p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .video-container {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    padding-bottom: 56.25%; /* 16:9 aspect ratio */
    margin-top: 1rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #000;
  }

  .video-container iframe {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border: none;
  }

  .coming-soon {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--color-background-alt);
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
